        fp: "Defendant was playing poker in a private backroom game when a fellow player accused Defendant of cheating. The player stood up, reached into his leather coat, and began pulling out a heavy steel revolver while shouting, 'I'm ending you right now!' Defendant instantly drew his own pistol and fired a shot, intending to shoot the player in the arm to disarm him. The bullet passed cleanly through the player's forearm, deflected off an iron radiator on the wall, and struck an innocent bystander who was watching the game from a couch, piercing the bystander's heart and killing him instantly. Medical testimony established that Defendant's shot was fired in lawful, necessary, and completely reasonable self-defense against the armed player. Defendant was charged with common law second-degree murder for the death of the bystander.",
